<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.530 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.530 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves were up at $1.530 billion on February 20, from $1.472 billion a week earlier, but lower than $2.258 billion on February 22, 1996, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It gave no reason for the rise. The reserves include $566 million within Pakistan and $284 million abroad, it said.</p>
<p>Pakistan's weekly foreign exchange reserves position:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		FEB 20     FEB 13     FEB 22, 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL 1,530 1,472 2,258</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	     566	  457	  1,122</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan	284	  335	    424</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion	676	  676	    705</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights	  4	    4		7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
